{"fag":{"id":"d63648c1-74c7-451a-9238-f8ae063f793f","word":"fag","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"homosexual man","tags":["Portugal","masculine"],"word":"paneleiro"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"homosexual man","tags":["Brazil","masculine"],"word":"viado"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"homosexual man","tags":["masculine"],"word":"boiola"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"homosexual man","tags":["feminine"],"word":"bicha"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"[1921 John Lind, The Female Impersonators (Historical Documentation of American Slang v. 1, A-G, edited by Jonathan E. Lighter (New York: Random House, 1994) page 716.\nAndrogynes known as “fairies,” “fags,” or “brownies.”]","id":"4ab81b5f-27a6-48df-be73-6e86e3039e12"},{"text":"In schizophrenics, however, the homosexual outlet is sooner or later ... ideas that strangers call them \"cs,\" \"fairy,\" \"woman,\" \"fag,\" \" fruit,\" etc.). ...","ref":"1926, American Neurological Association with New York Neurological Association et al., Journal of nervous and mental disease, volume 94, page 467:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[129,132]],"id":"68d7cf8d-ab71-4403-a94c-950d8a9a7098"},{"text":"When they pick out a set of clubs for him to rent, he is so indifferent and silent the freckled kid in charge stares at him as if he's a moron. The thought flits through his brain that Eccles is known as a fag and he has become the new pet.","ref":"1960, John Updike, 'Rabbit, Run', page 111:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[206,209]],"id":"e48d05a0-5b5a-48d8-85be-02e7484e9d34"},{"text":"A couple of days later, Trisha tells Madelyn there is a rumor going around that she's a fag.","ref":"2006, Lynn Mickelsen, Confusion Turned to Chaos:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[88,91]],"id":"401323b4-71f3-4ef7-a9c6-9ddd98e074dc"},{"text":"... what appeared to be overt appeals to anti-gay sentiment. When House Majority Whip Dick Armey referred to fellow Congressman Barney Frank as \"Barney Fag\" in 1995, he suffered a barage of negative publicity that prompted him to explain his choice of words as a slip of the tongue.","ref":"2008, Paul Ryan Brewer, Value war: public opinion and the politics of gay rights, →ISBN, page 60:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[152,155]],"id":"229104a5-8e8c-4fb6-b100-2b3a7158f05a"}],"categories":["American English","Canadian English","English endearing terms","English offensive terms","English terms with quotations","English vulgarities"],"links":[["endearing","endearing"],["homosexual","homosexual"],["man","man"]],"raw_glosses":["(US, Canada, vulgar, usually offensive, sometimes endearing) A homosexual man."],"glosses":["A homosexual man."],"tags":["Canada","US","endearing","offensive","sometimes","usually","vulgar"],"id":"dedc5ec6-93d4-4785-bd3d-c2836bd5b7d1"},{"categories":["English derogatory terms","English offensive terms","English slang"],"links":[["derogatory","derogatory"],["effeminate","effeminate"],["unusual","unusual"],["homosexual","homosexual"],["man","man"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang, offensive, usually derogatory) An effeminate or unusual homosexual man."],"glosses":["An effeminate or unusual homosexual man."],"tags":["derogatory","offensive","slang","usually"],"id":"bc7890dd-9166-47e4-8729-817c399f9f76"},{"examples":[{"text":"Why did you do that, you fag?","bold_text_offsets":[[25,28]],"type":"example","id":"77b537f6-7d19-47a1-b2a7-bc03efa606f3"}],"categories":["American English","English derogatory terms","English offensive terms","English terms with usage examples","English vulgarities"],"links":[["derogatory","derogatory"],["annoying","annoying"],["contemptible","contemptible"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"assbag","source":"Thesaurus:jerk"},{"word":"assbreath","source":"Thesaurus:jerk"},{"word":"assbucket","source":"Thesaurus:jerk"},{"word":"asscunt","source":"Thesaurus:jerk"},{"word":"assfa