ags":["masculine"],"word":"feixe"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"In the depth of, winter, however, a faggot of real French Sticks — although of little intrinsic value — may possibly enliven for a few moments an English Fireside.","ref":"1853, Sir Francis Bond Head, A faggot of French sticks: or, Paris in 1851, page 2:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[36,42]],"id":"04544f92-b025-4a21-a4ec-9e3e5561e879"},{"text":"Besides the logs and roots that simmered with turves and dung on the cottage fire, rapid heat for bread-making came from faggots - bundles of dry twigs about 4 ft long - which were fed into the oven, burned and then removed as ash before the dough went in.","ref":"1980, AA Book of British Villages, Drive Publications Ltd, page 118:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[121,128]],"id":"addd74f5-99d0-4568-8c83-0f5d6cd34b70"}],"senseid":["en:bundle"],"categories":["British English","English collective nouns","English terms with quotations","Irish English"],"links":[["bundle","bundle"],["sticks","sticks"],["brushwood","brushwood"],["fuel","fuel"],["withe","withe"],["bavin","bavin"]],"raw_glosses":["(chiefly UK, Ireland, collective) A bundle of sticks or brushwood intended to be used for fuel tied together for carrying. (Some sources specify that a faggot is tied with two bands or withes, whereas a bavin is tied with just one.)"],"glosses":["A bundle of sticks or brushwood intended to be used for fuel tied together for carrying. (Some sources specify that a faggot is tied with two bands or withes, whereas a bavin is tied with just one.)"],"tags":["Ireland","UK","collective","error-lua-timeout"],"id":"16a0ed6a-1c39-4f13-8240-f3bb7fe79deb"},{"categories":["English terms with obsolete senses"],"raw_glosses":["(obsolete) Burdensome baggage."],"glosses":["Burdensome baggage."],"tags":["error-lua-timeout","obsolete"],"id":"f815a936-c1de-487c-8e02-86e4ca46d7b9"},{"links":[["iron","iron"],["steel","steel"],["weld","weld"]],"glosses":["A bundle of pieces of iron or steel cut off into suitable lengths for welding."],"tags":["error-lua-timeout"],"id":"f4be834d-749c-43ae-989e-ce1f8a5df74a"},{"examples":[{"text":"He clambered back on his feet and grinned at them. The waning faggot cast red light over his fangs.","ref":"1961, Poul Anderson, Three Hearts and Three Lions:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[62,68]],"id":"8167116e-7e92-49db-ae14-0db9dcd0924b"},{"text":"To the east, the night grew a faggot of luminous gray, then seashell opalescence that dimmed the stars.","ref":"1965, Frank Herbert, Dune, New York: Ace Books, →OCLC, page 109:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[30,36]],"id":"df43b7ca-f744-4dcb-a171-07048fba22c7"}],"categories":["American English","English dated terms","English terms with quotations","English terms with rare senses","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["smouldering","smouldering"],["firewood","firewood"]],"raw_glosses":["(rare, dated in US) A burning or smouldering piece of firewood."],"glosses":["A burning or smouldering piece of firewood."],"tags":["dated","error-lua-timeout","rare"],"raw_tags":["in US"],"id":"6ad4de56-2a6e-4a5e-8f22-4a3a71816428"},{"examples":[{"text":"Today would be faggots in gravy and chocolate pudding with a white sauce. I didn't like faggots but picked at them and rolled the peas around my plate.","ref":"2008, Julie Hodgson, In My Father's Pockets, page 16:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[15,22],[88,95]],"id":"4171fbf7-6399-4eea-9656-5b5536ae9ab8"}],"categories":["British English","English terms with quotations","Irish English","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["meatball","meatball"],["offcut","offcut"],["offal","offal"],["pork","pork"],["Wikipedia","w:Faggot (food)"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"duck","tags":["obsolete","slang"]}],"raw_glosses":["(chiefly UK, Ireland) A meatball made with offcuts and offal, especially pork. (See Wikipedia.)"],"glosses":["A meatball made with offcuts and offal, especially pork. (See Wikipedia.)"],"tags":["Ireland","UK","error-lua-timeout"],"id":"ae187a3d-a847-449a-8912-4ae0bca2b97a"},{"examples":[{"text":"Drag, Example: “All the fagots (sissies) will be dressed in drag at the ball tonight.","ref":"1914, Louis E. Jackson and C.R. Hellyer, Vocabulary of Criminal Slang (Portland, OR: Modern Printing Co., 1914) page 30","id":"19fe8b62-b61e-4879-a734-d54487c7c91f"},{"text":"See the little faggot with the earring and the makeup? / Yeah buddy, that's his own hair / That little faggot got his own jet airplane / That little faggot, he's a millionaire","ref":"1985, Sting & Mark Knopfler, “Money for Nothing”, in Brothers in Arms, performed by Dire Straits:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[15,21],[103,109],[149,155]],"id":"157dfb93-5287-4fff-ac2f-ba1a9e0ccd18"},{"text":"Shortly after Surrey high school student Hamed Nastoh (called a “faggot” by classmates) killed himself by jumping off a bridge, James Chamberlain wrote a letter to the editor of a small newspaper called the Peace Arch News.","ref":"2000 June 28, Tom Yeung, “Using his death?”, in Xtra Magazine, archived from the original on 20 Apr 2024:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[65,71]],"id":"50784a28-7d76-442d-9c7f-674f5863b2f2"},{"text":"We're a hot looking crew that's your average faggot's wet dream, so we pull some pretty max tricks.","ref":"2004, Dennis Cooper, The Sluts, page 228:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[45,53]],"id":"e80b9099-2276-4579-aad7-b2ad2c71adfc"},{"text":"Fleissner's explanation presumably implies that Dickens meant Fag as an allusion to the derogatory English words fag 'homosexual', and faggot 'homosexual'","ref":"2009, David L. Gold, Studies in Etymology and Etiology, page 781:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[135,141]],"id":"0dc5d900-bdbb-41df-ae30-04f27a87010f"},{"text":"2012, Margaret Cho, quoted (mimicking Karl Lagerfeld) in On Making Sense: Queer Race Narratives of Intelligibility\nOf course I'm a faggot, darling. I'm a flaming faggot, darling. I am fanning the flames of my faggotry.","id":"7c13f7f0-40c4-41e7-966a-5e3f03aed812"}],"categories":["English derogatory terms","English offensive terms","English terms with quotations","English vulgarities","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["derogatory","derogatory"],["gay","gay"],["effeminate","effeminate"],["queer","queer"]],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"dyke"},{"word":"scissor sister"}],"raw_glosses":["(highly derogatory, offensive, vulgar) A gay man, especially an effeminate one; (by extension) a queer man."],"qualifier":"highly derogatory","glosses":["A gay man, especially an effeminate one; (by extension) a queer man."],"tags":["error-lua-timeout","offensive","vulgar"],"id":"5e477793-f761-4790-a714-a55074c8c596"},{"categories":["American English","Canadian English","English derogatory terms","English offensive terms","English vulgarities"],"links":[["derogatory","derogatory"],["man","man#Noun"],["effeminate","effeminate"]],"raw_glosses":["(chiefly US, Canada, derogatory, offensive, vulgar) A man considered effeminate."],"glosses":["A man considered effeminate."],"tags":["Canada","US","derogatory","error-lua-timeout","offensive","vulgar"],"id":"fa33258f-fa61-456e-b8ba-f6cbd3e942e2"},{"categories":["American English","Canadian English","English derogatory terms","English offensive terms","English vulgarities"],"links":[["derogatory","derogatory"],["inconsiderate","inconsiderate"],["contemptible","contemptible"]],"raw_glosses":["(US, Canada, derogatory, offensive, vulgar) An annoying, inconsiderate or contemptible person."],"glosses":["An annoying, inconsiderate or contemptible person."],"tags":["Canada","US","derogatory","error-lua-timeout","offensive","vulgar"],"id":"2fcab5c2-0c74-4009-854f-a0f095881d8a"},{"examples":[{"text":"I appoynt thée no more continencie, than to eate while thy bellie is full, nor conﬅancie, but to brawle rather than burne: a filbert is better than a faggot, except it be an Athenian ſhe handfull: you know that Coſmoſophos, euer ſince your laﬅ mariage, how doth the father of your ſonne in law?","ref":"1591, T[homas] L[odge] of Lincolns, Catharos Diogenes in his Singularitie: Wherein is comprehended his merrie baighting fit for all mens benefits: Christened by him, A Nettle for Nice Noſes, London: Iohn Busbie, page 12; republished [Glasgow]: [Hunterian Club], [1875]:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[150,156]],"id":"f0f78ba6-2127-4250-9226-6090f4509a64"},{"text":"she wants me to go to bed to her, and I won't, ... for she is as crooked as a ram's horn ... and as ugly as sin besides ; rot her, the dirty little faggot, she torments me.","ref":"1796, Theobald Wolfe Tone, Autobiography:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[148,154]],"id":"5de74e35-1740-4748-a43d-1fc8d7181d10"},{"text":"The woman, in accordance with the custom of the country, raised the Irish cry, in a loud melancholy wail ...\nDarby, who prided himself on maintaining silence, could not preserve the consistency of his character upon this occasion ... \"Your sowl to the divil, you faggot!\" he exclaimed, \"what do you mane? The divil whip the tongue out o' you! ...\"","ref":"1834, William Carleton, The Midnight Mass:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[263,269]],"id":"ae49c796-e4dd-4453-9ae6-d3e4ffe6a3c6"},{"text":"he used to be pretending to be laid up with a sick voice doing his highness to make himself interesting for that old faggot Mrs Riordan that he thought he had a great leg of and she never left us a farthing all for masses for herself and her soul greatest miser ever was actually afraid to lay out 4d for her methylated spirit […]","ref":"1922, James Joyce, chapter 18, in Ulysses:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[117,123]],"id":"a495afc6-1b6c-4bcd-9d5e-65048858ebde"},{"text":"To me she is fractious, tiresome, and a faggot. Yet the subtle desirableness is in her, for me. As it is in the brown hen, or even a sow.","ref":"1925, D. H. Lawrence, Reflections on the Death of a Porcupine and Other Essays: .. Love Was Once a Little Boy:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[40,46]],"id":"45bc6d72-0900-4479-a673-b207dcb4ae11"},{"text":"MOTHER: To see who?\nDA: You faggot, you; don't let on you don't know.","ref":"1973, Hugh Leonard, Da:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[28,34]],"id":"ee3c7348-57ea-481d-a270-31f8d37b8c2e"}],"categories":["British English","English colloquialisms","English derogatory terms","English offensive terms","English terms with archaic senses","English terms with quotations","Irish English","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["derogatory","derogatory"],["old","old"],["shrewish","shrewish"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"battle axe","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"bitch","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"brim","source":"Thesaurus:shrew","tags":["UK","slang"]},{"word":"brimstone","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"cat","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"crow","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"dragon","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"faggot","source":"Thesaurus:shrew","tags":["Ireland","UK","obsolete"]},{"word":"fishwife","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"harpy","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"harridan","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"hellcat","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"jade","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"nag","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"nudnik","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"scold","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"she-devil","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"shrew","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"termagant","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"virago","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"vixen","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"},{"word":"witch","source":"Thesaurus:shrew"}],"raw_glosses":["(UK, Ireland, archaic, colloquial, derogatory, now offensive) An old and/or shrewish woman."],"glosses":["An old and/or shrewish woman."],"tags":["Ireland","UK","archaic","colloquial","derogatory","error-lua-timeout","offensive"],"id":"3639bb52-7eca-4501-